Fix APC's malformed request bodies, move the Service Live/Cached badge
above the dropdown (v0.129)

Dan reported that on v0.128, picking an APC service showed "Not live for
this address: Failed to check APC service availability - APC said:
UNEXPECTED ERROR" - and that whatever changed was blocking every live
APC service lookup, not just this one address.

Re-read the APC Hypaship API v3 integration guide's own literal JSON/XML
request examples (booking and service-availability calls both use the
same envelope). Root cause: ApcShippingService built its request bodies
as flat JSON at the root, but APC's actual schema requires the whole
payload wrapped as {"Orders": {"Order": {...}}}. ShipmentDetails.Items
was also the wrong shape - a bare array - where APC wants
{"Items": {"Item": {...}}} for a single item or
{"Items": {"Item": [{...}, {...}]}} for several, with the array nested
one level inside "Item", not "Items" itself being an array.

This had been silently wrong since the very first APC integration in
v0.126 - APC was rejecting every booking and service-availability call
outright with an "UNEXPECTED ERROR" the whole time. It only became
visible once v0.128's Messages.Code check started actually surfacing
APC's real response instead of treating HTTP 200 as success regardless
of body content. Both buildRequestBody() and buildServiceAvailabilityBody()
now wrap the payload correctly via a shared wrapAsOrder() helper; booking
and label response parsing were loosened from checking one fixed nesting
level to searching the whole response (findPath), in case APC's replies
use the same wrapper.

Also moved the Service dropdown's small "Live"/"Cached" badge (APC and
DPD both use the same pattern) from an absolutely-positioned overlay on
top of the select box to its own row just above it, next to the
"Service" label, per Dan's request - it no longer sits over the
dropdown text and doesn't push any surrounding layout around.

